            <ArticleTitle>Osteoarthritis: priorities for osteoarthritis research: much to be done.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>447-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrrheum.2014.76</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With a frustrating lack of progress in the development of treatments for osteoarthritis, EULAR has released recommendations to reorient research into this disease. These recommendations include focused attention on noncartilagenous tissues, the interaction of structures within the joint, the pathogenesis of osteoarthritic pain, new treatment strategies and early disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
